WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.750
Okay.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:02.870
This is really important.

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:10.590
The Trump administration has documents showing
they know how many people might die if states

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.080
open too quickly.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.990
It's a big number and those documents have
now leaked.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.730
Of course, the Trump administration is not
talking publicly about any of this.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:24.060
So when we ask the question how many people
will die of coronavirus, there is not one

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.060
answer.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.619
A, we have modeling their confidence intervals.

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:33.420
The death toll depends on things that we can't
control, like how contagious is coronavirus?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.260
What is the bottom line?

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.260
Death rate.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.250
The fatality rate of the virus.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:43.000
The death toll also depends on things we can
control, like social distancing, whether we

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.500
open states too early, whether we find a treatment
or a vaccine.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.700
Now, publicly, the Trump administration has
taken the approach of claiming that the baseline,

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.960
if he did nothing, would have been 2.2 million
deaths.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.379
Trump often says, I could have done nothing
and to 2.2 million people would have died,

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:00.379
but I've done stuff.

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:01.969
So we're gonna be way below that now.

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:05.229
No president could really get away with doing
nothing.

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:09.020
Once you start mitigation, the possible death
toll starts to decline.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.120
One model said could be one hundred and fifty
to two hundred and fifty thousand.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.150
Another said could be one to two hundred thousand.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:18.960
And eventually, as more and more governors
closed down, projections kept improving, down

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.909
to roughly 60 to 70 thousand deaths for wave
one in which we are right now.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:28.509
The wave one thing is important because more
and more medical experts think there will

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:33.560
be a second wave of the virus starting in
the fall, possibly a third wave in 2021.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.590
OK, let's put that aside for now.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:41.290
The important question now is, after going
through weeks of mitigation, what would happen

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.549
if we reopen states too early?

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.940
We had a record single day death toll this
week.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.190
We are have very high numbers of deaths.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:52.869
We are still finding 25000 or more new cases
every single day in the United States.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:54.070
We're hopefully in the peak.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.070
The peak is a plateau.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.050
It can last a month or so.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.479
If we do everything right.

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:03.399
So when Texas and Georgia and other states
plan to reopen tomorrow and Monday and other

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:05.259
days next week, it's very risky.

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:07.500
Now, Trump was asked a few days ago.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.340
Are you worried about a resurgence in the
virus if states open too quickly?

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.709
Have you modeled what those numbers would
look like?

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:17.500
And Trump said, if we did nothing, we would
have lost 2 million people.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.620
Now we won't.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:24.480
The truth, though, is we know that they do
have models about what happens if they open

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.569
too early and they're really, really bad.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:29.819
Before we look at the models, here's Trump's
answer when he was asked about this a few

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:31.300
days ago.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.720
Thank you.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.890
Has the government modeled the possibility
that there is a widespread resurgence if this

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:41.020
just doesn't work?

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.150
How many deaths?

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.480
So if we didn't do what we did.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.430
We were talking about up to 2.2 million deaths.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:54.450
So that's five times almost what we lost in
the civil war.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.580
Okay.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:01.360
If if everything happens properly and if we
continue to go the way we're going now, we

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.489
will be significantly less than the lowest
number with mitigation.

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:09.069
So we'll be significantly less.

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:11.150
And it's still a lot of people.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.659
Now, Trump, first of all, didn't answer saying
if I did nothing, we would have 2.2 million

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:16.659
deaths.

00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:20.580
The question was, have you modeled what would
happen if you open too early?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.090
The answer is a simple yes.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.880
And we have those models.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:30.459
Trump gave that ridiculous answer on April
17th, but in early April, the federal government

00:03:30.459 --> 00:03:35.030
put together models of what happens if social
distancing stops too quickly and the numbers

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.420
are anywhere from a middle of the road.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.470
Guess of 300000 thousand deaths all the way
up to 1.8 million deaths.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.459
This is a model from the Department of Health
and Human Services.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:49.950
Trump's administration had the data in early
April, but Trump gave a bogus answer.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.830
We now have their models and they are very
concerning.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.569
The Department of HHS has four scenarios and
then they have like a best guess, which is

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:58.640
in the middle.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:05.800
The models range from 94000 deaths, up to
1.8 million deaths.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:11.470
Trump likes to say thanks to me, we'll have
60000 deaths instead of 2.2 million.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:17.450
It's absurd, but thanks to opening too early,
you could have 1.8 million deaths instead

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.040
of 60000.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.540
The best scenario, expect 94000 deaths.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:28.940
There are some in-between models up all the
way up to one which they pegged at 1.8 million

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:29.940
deaths.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:34.290
And then you have a sort of average of these
a best guess right now, which says if you

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:39.330
open to early, about 300000 people are going
to die.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.800
So there are multiple things to think about
here.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.780
First, Trump was asked, have you modeled this?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.160
And he didn't answer.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.759
It's possible he saw this model, but he won't
admit it.

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:49.570
That's a problem of dishonesty.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.120
It's possible he didn't even see it.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:55.370
That's a problem of Trump often not having
the facts because he lacks the attention span

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.610
to actually absorb that information.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:04.840
Number two, if Trump wants to take credit
for 60K instead of 2 million, he would have

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:10.389
to take responsibility for 300K K or a million
or 1.8 million instead of 60k.

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:15.070
If it's a result of states opening to early
thanks to his public posturing about opening

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:19.170
up the economy over the last 24 hours, he
has finally said, you know, I think maybe

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:23.650
George is opening up too early and it's possible
someone got to him and said, you can't be

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.930
on the side of encouraging this because it's
going to be really bad.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.200
But the most important takeaway is the government
has the data.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.800
They know the risks and they have the numbers.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:37.789
And yet Trump and Fox News have mostly still
been fomenting these freedom and liberty protests

00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:42.050
around the country from people just demanding
that governors let it rip.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.139
People will die.

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:45.240
We now know that they know it.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.460
And the next thing I want to talk.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:50.800
About is the astro turfed protesters that
we have seen

